#
# Preference — BY-REFERENCE composition bridges. The preference slice is a CORE
# CONSUMER: it mints its own bridge vocabulary and composes vocabulary it does
# not own. Each row below documents one such reuse: a preference term relates to
# the term it composes with, so the composition is a shipped, auditable
# correspondence rather than an implicit dependency. Compiled to
# mappings/gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv by `gmeow compile-mappings`.
#
# EVERY ROW HERE TARGETS A CORE TERM. That is a tier constraint, not a style
# choice: a mapping artifact is a SEMANTIC dependency edge (purrdf
# EdgeKind::Mapping), so a cell naming an extension's term would BE a core ->
# extension dependency, which Principle 16 forbids however the cell is phrased.
# The observations (EvaluationVerdict, Condition), ai (ModelInvocation, Prompt),
# learning (LearningEvent), provenance (wasDerivedFrom), and evidence
# (EvidenceSpan) targets below are all core, so each is a legal reference.
#
# The gmeow:usesRubric -> gmeow:Rubric and gmeow:onCriterion -> gmeow:Criterion
# seams carry NO row by design: observations is a core slice preference declares
# in gmeow:sliceDependsOn, so those two seams are carried by real rdfs:range
# axioms in module.ttl and a correspondence row would be a second source of truth.
#
# Two further reuses carry NO cell, and deliberately so — see the trailer on
# gmeow:mapsetPreference for the model-serving gmeow:ModelArtifact and the
# semantic-topology gmeow:TopologyClaim, both of which are extensions.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .

gmeow:mapsetPreference a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/preference" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment "By-reference composition bridges from the core preference slice to the CORE vocabulary it composes: the observations evaluative primitives (EvaluationVerdict, Condition), ai (ModelInvocation, Prompt), learning (LearningEvent), provenance (wasDerivedFrom), and evidence (EvidenceSpan). Each row documents an instance-level reuse (Principle 5 / Principle 16), NOT a redeclaration: the preference slice composes the term, it does not re-mint it. Every target is core, because a mapping cell is a semantic dependency edge and a core slice may not depend on an extension. The gmeow:usesRubric → gmeow:Rubric and gmeow:onCriterion → gmeow:Criterion bridges are absent by design — observations is a core slice preference declares in gmeow:sliceDependsOn, so those two seams are carried by real rdfs:range axioms in module.ttl and a correspondence row would be a second source of truth." ;
    gmeow:setTrailer "# NO CELL for the two EXTENSION reuses (Principle 16 — a mapping artifact is a semantic dependency edge, so a cell naming an extension's term would BE the forbidden core -> extension crossing, however the cell is phrased):\n# gmeow:deltaBaseArtifact\tskos:relatedMatch\tgmeow:ModelArtifact\tmodel-serving\tthe checkpoint a config delta is a change FROM. deltaBaseArtifact ranges over the CORE gmeow:InformationObject and is never a range axiom against model-serving; the reuse is instance-level and is demonstrated where the tier model allows it — examples/model-delta-worked.ttl types ex:baseCkpt gmeow:ModelArtifact, and tests/counter-examples/duplicate-model-serving-term.ttl guards the no-re-mint ban.\n# gmeow:DisagreementObstruction\tskos:relatedMatch\tgmeow:TopologyClaim\tsemantic-topology\tthe H1 twin. What the two share is not each other but the math: sheaf apparatus they each compose independently: DisagreementObstruction wraps a math:GluingObstruction (gmeow:obstructionClass) exactly as ConsensusSection wraps a math:GlobalSection, under the same H0/H1 gluing picture TopologyClaim governs. That shared substrate is already shipped as an axiom and PROVED by queries/competency/cq-cross-slice-compose-semantic-topology.rq, which composes through math: and names no semantic-topology term." .

# ── observations (core): verdict / contract value vocabulary, by-reference ────
gmeow:verifierOutcome skos:relatedMatch gmeow:EvaluationVerdict {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.8 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:verifierOutcome ranges over the grounding logic:QualityValue and reuses the core observations gmeow:EvaluationVerdict value vocabulary (verdictHeld / verdictNotHeld / verdictUndetermined) by reference at the instance level (Principle 16), rather than minting a parallel verdict axis."
|} .

gmeow:verifierContract skos:relatedMatch gmeow:Condition {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.75 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:verifierContract ranges over the core gmeow:InformationObject — a verifier contract is any information object, not specifically a gmeow:Condition — and reaches the core observations condition apparatus by reference (via the norms gmeow:formalizedAs) at the instance level: the contract a verdict verifies against."
|} .

# ── ai: model invocation and prompt, reused by-reference ──────────────────────
gmeow:candidateGeneratedBy skos:relatedMatch gmeow:ModelInvocation {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.85 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:candidateGeneratedBy reuses the ai gmeow:ModelInvocation by reference (Principle 16) — the invocation that minted a candidate, joining ordinary provenance queries rather than re-grounding generation."
|} .

gmeow:deltaPromptIdentity skos:relatedMatch gmeow:Prompt {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.85 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:deltaPromptIdentity reuses the ai gmeow:Prompt by reference (Principle 16) — the exact prompt leg of a model-config delta's identity tuple, never a re-minted prompt vocabulary."
|} .

# ── learning: the learning event, specialized by-reference ────────────────────
gmeow:PreferenceLearningEvent skos:narrowMatch gmeow:LearningEvent {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.9 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:PreferenceLearningEvent specializes the learning gmeow:LearningEvent — it reuses the shipped learning-event term by reference (Principle 16) rather than minting a parallel training vocabulary; a preference-learning run IS a kind of learning event, so the alignment is skos:narrowMatch (the preference term is strictly narrower than the learning-slice term), not a symmetric closeMatch."
|} .

# ── provenance: the derivation spine, reused by-reference ──────────────────────
gmeow:recordsProjectionPreservation skos:relatedMatch gmeow:wasDerivedFrom {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.75 ;
    gmeow:comment "compiling observations into a sheaf is a projection whose preservation/loss ledger rides the provenance derivation spine — gmeow:recordsProjectionPreservation composes with gmeow:wasDerivedFrom by reference (Principle 16 / Principle 17), never re-minting the provenance vocabulary."
|} .

# ── evidence: the evidence span, reused by-reference ──────────────────────────
gmeow:deltaEvaluationEvidence skos:relatedMatch gmeow:EvidenceSpan {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-preference.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.85 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:deltaEvaluationEvidence reuses the evidence gmeow:EvidenceSpan by reference (Principle 16) — the evidence leg that makes a config delta's evaluation warrant auditable, never a re-minted evidence term."
|} .
